course: dictionary
lesson: 4680
title: Holy and its clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Holy is an adjective: it describes something. Holy means special because it is connected with God or a religion, and people treat it with deep respect. The words around it give you clues: «holy books» and «holy places» are things people look after with care.
explain: Read this: «Christians remember the Last Supper in Holy Communion.» Communion is a religious service, so holy tells you it is sacred to Christians. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try special or religious, then check the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Holy can also describe a person who is very religious and good. But «Holy cow!» is different. The surprise in the words and the exclamation mark tell you it is a cry of surprise, not a talk about a cow. Context shows you which meaning is right.
fact: Holy means special because it is connected with God or a religion.
fact: Holy books include the Bible, the Qur'an and the Torah.
fact: The Holy Spirit is one of the three persons of the Trinity in Christianity: the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit.
fact: «Holy cow!» and «Holy moly!» are informal cries of surprise.
fact: The comparison forms of holy are holier and holiest.
exercise: «The Trinity means one God in three persons: the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit.» What does holy mean in «Holy Spirit»? | Very old and dusty | Wet and grey | *Special, connected with God | Loud and happy
exercise: Max shouts «Holy cow!» when he sees a rainbow. What does this show? | Hunger | Sleepiness | *Surprise | A cow in a field
exercise: In «holy places», what kind of word is holy? | A noun | An adverb | *An adjective | A verb
test: «Pentecostal churches are named after Pentecost, when the Holy Spirit came on the first disciples.» In this sentence, holy means | Very tired | Very angry | *Special and connected with God | Shiny and new
test: Which word is the comparison form meaning more holy? | Holiest | *Holier | Holyest | Most holyer
exam: In a court, a witness may swear on a «holy book» to tell «the whole truth». What does holy book mean? | *A book that is special to a religion | A book full of jokes | A very old book that is falling apart | A book about cooking
